meta {
  name: Assign Departments
  type: http
  seq: 22
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/users/manage/{{manageUserId}}/departments
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "departmentIds": ["{{departmentId}}", "{{departmentId2}}"],
    "defaultDepartmentId": "{{departmentId}}"
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  manageUserId: 204f8ce7-17e0-4251-b575-5f1b6255c8f8
  departmentId:
  departmentId2:
}

docs {
  Assign (replace) the set of departments a staff user belongs to (tenant-wide),
  marking one as the user's default. Send the **full desired set** every time:
  departments not listed are removed, new ones are added.

  Storage reuses the shared `department_person_mappings` table with `type = USER`
  and `branch_id = NULL`. The write is a **diff**, not a blunt replace:
  - departments already mapped are updated in place (only `is_default`), so any
    `position` / `priority` / `is_signatory` set by the Department form on a
    shared `(person, department, USER)` row is preserved;
  - newly-selected departments are created with a generic default position
    (`TECHNICIAN`, `priority = 1`) — those fields aren't captured by this flow;
  - deselected departments are soft-deleted.

  At most one department is the user's default; `defaultDepartmentId` (optional)
  must be one of `departmentIds` else 422 DEFAULT_DEPARTMENT_NOT_SELECTED. Every
  id must be an active department of the caller's tenant else 422
  INVALID_DEPARTMENT_ASSIGNMENT. 404 STAFF_MEMBERSHIP_NOT_FOUND if the person is
  not a staff member. An empty `departmentIds` clears all assignments.

  Returns `{ departmentIds, defaultDepartmentId }` — the persisted set.
}
